    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The mainland half of the old Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a>, ruled separately from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicilian-vespers">Sicilian Vespers</a> of 1282.</li><li>Angevin, Aragonese, Spanish and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-bourbon">Bourbon</a> rulers made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a> one of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>'s largest cities and a centre of art and learning.</li><li>Its feudal baronage and heavy taxes fuelled revolts; in 1816 it merged with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a> into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-two-sicilies">Kingdom of the Two Sicilies</a>.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Though ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a>, the kingdom officially kept the name Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a> while the island had kings of its own, which is why their union in 1816 was called the Two Sicilies.</p></aside>
    </section>

